WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.442 --> 00:00:06.275
- Ah.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:08.550
- Here we go, perfect.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.390
- [Mark] All right, Ernie.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:27.810
Ernie, where'd you grow up?

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.740
Where are you from? Originally?

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:30.740
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.763
- Cuba and New Mexico.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.290
White Horse Lake.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.033
- [Mark] In New Mexico?

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.360
- Yeah.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.417
- [Mark] And tell me about your family.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:46.473
You're Navajo?

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:49.963
- My mom's Navajo.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.062
But my dad's a Cheyenne Native.

00:00:54.062 --> 00:00:56.108
- [Mark] Cheyenne?

00:00:56.108 --> 00:00:59.973
- North of, north of Cheyenne.
That's where my dad's from.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:03.403
But they like each other.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.943
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:10.850
- I don't know what's going on.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.120
But mom's gone.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.350
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.113
- I came into town,

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:19.403
started drinking.

00:01:20.456 --> 00:01:21.789
I'm feeling ham.

00:01:22.942 --> 00:01:24.753
- [Mark] When did you
start drinking alcohol?

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.193
- Oh, my first time?

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.359
I was 13 years old.

00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:33.850
- [Mark] Thirteen.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.703
- Mama had her bar in the home.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.773
I didn't know.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.603
That was in Denver.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:50.223
Her and my dad, they had their bar open.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.503
Then one day,

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.900
I had a friend.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.723
It was a hot boy on the
side, on the street.

00:02:04.872 --> 00:02:06.789
(Sigh)

00:02:09.101 --> 00:02:11.434
(Inaudible)

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.610
They left. Hey, my mom left,

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.023
for the weekend.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.263
I didn't drink nothing.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:27.273
Then the little boy came by.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:31.690
He said "Why, why don't
you try that whiskey?".

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:38.330
And we did. That's why I started to drink.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:39.623
- [Mark] Whiskey, at 13?

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.293
What is your drink-

00:02:42.293 --> 00:02:43.126
- I-

00:02:43.126 --> 00:02:43.963
- [Mark] What is your drink today?

00:02:45.995 --> 00:02:48.028
- (inaudible)

00:02:48.028 --> 00:02:49.023
- [Mark] Vodka?

00:02:50.543 --> 00:02:52.643
- Well, now it's turned to Vodka.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:56.810
- [Mark] Could you drink
some of the other things

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.690
that people will use to get drunk?

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:02.163
Like, like hairspray
and Gatorade or Lysol?

00:03:03.083 --> 00:03:04.384
Or what else, what other
stuff, what other things

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.217
did you-

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:07.427
- I stole it!

00:03:07.427 --> 00:03:08.663
- [Mark] You stole what?

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.020
- Hairspray, Lysol.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.940
I did all that stuff.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:19.421
- [Mark] You drink it? It
gets you, it gets you drunk?

00:03:19.421 --> 00:03:22.163
- Huh? (inaudible)

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:25.720
- [Mark] What about
like, things like perfume

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.291
or rubbing alcohol?

00:03:27.291 --> 00:03:29.543
- I did it. I did it.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.770
- [Mark] What's the
difference between vodka and

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.732
and rubbing alcohol, or perfume?

00:03:35.732 --> 00:03:36.565
- Uh...

00:03:36.565 --> 00:03:38.160
- [Mark] Or Lysol.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:38.993
- Same thing.

00:03:38.993 --> 00:03:41.218
- [Mark] Same thing?
It just gets you high?

00:03:41.218 --> 00:03:42.470
- Gets drunk.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:43.303
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.190
And you sleep on the street?

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.390
It gets cold at night, no?

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:49.593
- No. I've been on the street.

00:03:49.593 --> 00:03:51.490
- [Mark] Oh, in the
winter it gets very cold

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:52.490
there in New Mexico.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:55.573
- Yep.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.830
People die sometimes from that, right?

00:03:58.830 --> 00:03:59.663
- I know.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:06.180
But, I did all that,

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.483
and I'm trying to go home.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:18.510
I'm (inaudible)

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.050
- [Mark] What do you do for money?

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.523
How do you, how do you get money?

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:24.503
- Just every day-

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:26.983
- [Mark] You just panhandle?

00:04:26.983 --> 00:04:27.967
- Drinking.

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.480
- [Mark] But you pan,
you ask people, you-you-

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:32.496
you beg for money and
people give it to you?

00:04:32.496 --> 00:04:33.447
- I make money.

00:04:33.447 --> 00:04:35.550
- [Mark] How do you make money?

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:36.383
- Panhandle.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:41.760
I make money and then...

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:45.663
some days is good, and other days not.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:48.163
- [Mark] Do you have children?

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.023
- I have nobody.

00:04:51.896 --> 00:04:53.646
- [Mark] No family, no friends, no?

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.187
- I only have one. My sister.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:04.643
- [Mark] Your sister's all you have left?

00:05:07.482 --> 00:05:11.649
- (crying) I have my brother too.

00:05:15.604 --> 00:05:20.604
I just drink.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:34.280
My brother's quarantined
over there at that Motel.

00:05:35.596 --> 00:05:38.983
He's supposed to get
out today or tomorrow.

00:05:43.125 --> 00:05:46.450
- [Mark] Did you once
live on a reservation?

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.283
- Huh?

00:05:47.283 --> 00:05:49.870
- [Mark] Did you once live
on an Indian reservation?

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.837
- Nah, I had a reservation. Mine.

00:05:52.837 --> 00:05:55.093
It's, it's different.

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:00.683
We pay for our lands.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.423
I'm not on the reservation.

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:10.023
I paid for my lands,

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.433
where I live.

00:06:17.168 --> 00:06:18.753
These guys, Arizona.

00:06:21.517 --> 00:06:23.283
They don't pay nothing for it.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.050
But I paid for mine.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.113
Then now,

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:37.817
we got oil, whatever.

00:06:40.606 --> 00:06:42.023
Oil, coal, water.

00:06:43.643 --> 00:06:45.713
That's all we got to pay with now.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:58.253
And then I'll go out to,
my dad's from Montana.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:03.240
- [Mark] The Cheyenne part of your family?

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:04.740
- We're fighters, (inaudible)!

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.573
- I don't know if you guys know.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.360
We don't, we don't retreat.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.570
We don't retreat, I said.

00:07:18.686 --> 00:07:20.503
Shit, I don't know.

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:23.833
We fight.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.034
My uncles and...

00:07:29.034 --> 00:07:31.117
(crying)

00:07:37.715 --> 00:07:40.048
(inaudible)

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:45.510
They said that we...

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.510
Um...

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:04.850
But they blame...

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:12.553
I didn't make (inaudible) with my Aunt.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:17.033
They killed her out there!

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:23.430
They threw her in the pit, in the wash.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:25.810
Some wash out there.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:28.160
- [Mark] She died in the, on the street?

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:29.904
- Yep. They killed her!

00:08:29.904 --> 00:08:31.403
- [Mark] Oh, they killed her?

00:08:31.403 --> 00:08:33.437
- Cause she would,

00:08:33.437 --> 00:08:35.104
she stood up for us!

00:08:38.763 --> 00:08:41.273
They found her body over there.

00:08:44.243 --> 00:08:46.910
And now my brother's over there.

00:08:47.865 --> 00:08:50.198
(inaudible)

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:57.427
- Yep. I'm not scared.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:02.243
They can kill me.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:06.303
I'm not giving (inaudible)
to the Government.

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:11.883
They know me. They know my family!

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:17.747
We're (inaudible)!

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:22.070
I can't...

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:24.423
They can kill me, I don't care.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.447
They did it to my grandma too!

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:33.500
My grandma!

00:09:40.575 --> 00:09:42.742
(sobbing)

00:09:44.203 --> 00:09:45.036
Grandma.

00:09:50.055 --> 00:09:52.222
(sobbing)

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:56.670
- [Mark] For many reasons, it's
hard to be Native American,

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:57.801
isn't it today?

00:09:57.801 --> 00:09:58.980
(cries out)

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:00.823
- We have our rights!

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.670
We're not scared!

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:08.670
I'm not scared of them. They
can fucking kill me right now.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:11.426
I'm ready for it.

00:10:11.426 --> 00:10:14.699
(heavy breathing)

00:10:14.699 --> 00:10:16.616
I'm not scared of them.

00:10:21.379 --> 00:10:23.000
(crying)

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:25.103
I don't know what they did to my family.

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:30.213
But, they're gone.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.683
And I'm done here!

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:47.323
My mom! My mom's family on this side.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:55.794
- [Mark] Okay Ernie, well
thank you for talking with me.

00:10:55.794 --> 00:10:56.627
Appreciate it.

00:10:56.627 --> 00:10:58.863
- Well, it's right there.

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:02.220
- [Mark] Thank you.

